From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] shell32, explorer: New offers the file types programs register

A program offers a new empty document in the shell's New menu by a
ShellNew key (HKCR\.ext\ProgID\ShellNew or HKCR\.ext\ShellNew: NullFile,
Data or FileName). SG Office registers .docx, .xlsx and .pptx so, but the
New menus -- File Explorer's command bar, the folder view's right-click menu,
the desktop's -- had only Folder and Text Document. They list the types by
name now and make "New <type name>.ext" as the key says, numbered if taken.
---
--- /dev/null
+++ b/include/wine/sgshellnew.h
@@ -0,0 +1,184 @@
+/*
+ * Stained Glass OS: the New menu's file types (ShellNew)
+ *
+ * A program offers a new empty document of its type in the shell's New menu
+ * by a ShellNew key: HKCR\.ext\ProgID\ShellNew (the extension's ProgID) or
+ * HKCR\.ext\ShellNew, with NullFile (an empty file), Data (the file's bytes)
+ * or FileName (a template, in %SystemRoot%\ShellNew when not a full path).
+ * The menu says the type's name (the ProgID's default value) and the file
+ * is "New <type name>.ext", numbered if taken. File Explorer's command bar,
+ * the folder view's right-click menu and the desktop's use these.
+ *
